hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to the  edition of ask Evan today I'm gonna  answer a question from one of my  newsletter readers dieter who wrote in  saying Evan could you tell us about your  tough times right now you have a  beautiful life we always read about your  success into determination but how did  successful people like you come through  the tough times did you cry bake run hug  somebody thank you so much dieter a  great question and I think if you look  at any successful entrepreneur you have  to go through a whole bunch of tough  time fuel to get to the end goal and I  think it really helped me when I was  first getting started it was it was  tough in that was making autumn asst  takes and I wasn't really quite sure  what I wanted to do I knew I wanted to  help entrepreneurs and that was a  passion that I had but I didn't really  know what the model was and that's a big  challenge with a lot of entrepreneurs  face when you're starting up what's the  business model going to be right how you  gonna make money it's great that you're  helping people and you're following your  passion but to make it sustainable you  have to be able to make a living from it  right you have to be able to make enough  at least to get past survival so you're  paying your bills and then you can  continue to grow from there luckily for  me I had a lot of encouragement from  friends and family a lot i know a lot of  entrepreneurs don't have that you know  their family doesn't believe in them  they don't think there should be an  entrepreneur their friends are jealous  and you know put them down so I had a  lot of support around me which is great  but still it was really tough getting it  going you know the first the first part  of running a business is so hard because  you want things happen so badly and it  takes a while to get going and you put  so much work in I think a lot of  entrepreneurs just quit too soon you put  so much working at the beginning and you  invest so much time and energy and then  you don't see the immediate results and  then you quit and its really driving  force that you do something every single  day to make your business grow even just  a little bit and you eventually see that  momentum start to take shape and you'll  be able to build it into a successful  enterprise so what helped me was getting  feedback from  my customers my entrepreneurs were  getting the stuff that was creating and  just looking at the feedback and seeing  you know what I'm doing is actually  helping people and what I found swish at  the beginning most of the stuff that I  did at the start was offline it wasn't  to my website was through seminars  presentations to entrepreneur groups  sharing different you know topics  lessons that I had learned from my  success in business and what I found  interesting there was you go to an event  like that and I love speaking so you go  to a speaking event and you get all  jazzed up you get all excited you see  how you're helping people and you're in  that moment and you want to go home and  work like crazy to you know get to  another moment like that and then you  wake up the next day and it's gone and  how do you keep that momentum going you  know you don't want to just stay in bed  all day so how do you get the momentum  going between those highs and what I  found helpful was I made a actual little  presentation powerpoint that I watched  every day in the morning just for a  couple minutes that had some of the  quotes that people had left on their  feedback form so at the end of all the  presentations I did I had these little  feedback forms to ask people what they  thought and how can make it better and  the reviews that came back were awesome  you know people talked about how it  changed their life and how gave them  such helpful information are going to go  home and take action it's really  inspiring that's the part that I really  love about my business and so instead of  just having that high that one night I  put it together in that presentation it  was very simple just something I loaded  up every day and put a song to it and it  kind of got me going in the morning  caught me sinking you know I've been  able to help these people and I want to  do it again and I want to you know we  live that moment again and help more  people now or at the point within my  business where I get emails every day  from people who are saying how much they  really liked the video we made or the  newsletter or the content on our website  and even on YouTube getting the likes  and get in the comment is awesome that's  the stuff that makes you want to do more  of these videos and keeps me going every  day is your comments it's not so much  the money that comes in it's it's the  feeling that you're helping people and  how can they go through times that could  be tough I'm just having somebody who  believes in you it can be a really  powerful thing and so I found that  really helpful so in terms of I don't  know where you're at with your business  sounds like you're still kind of in the  earlies days I try to tap into the  feeling that you're helping people  because if you're motivated only by  money it makes it really hard to keep  going you know you're going to quit as  soon as it gets really really hard if  you're not really interested in what  you're doing and you don't feel like  you're helping people you can fight it  for so long you can fight it saying well  I'm going to make a lot of money doing  this but the money usually doesn't come  right away it comes after a lot a lot a  lot of hard work and effort so what I  would encourage you to do is think about  how you're really helping people and try  to remember those stories so think about  the best part you have in your business  whatever the the greatest high you've  had in your your company it was probably  something around helping somebody you  know really solve a frustration a  problem that they were facing and just  try to relive that moment every day or  every week as much as you can to get  yourself back into that zone of wanting  to get motivated and do a lot of work  and build this business up and tie back  into that vision that you have for the  company the second thing I thought  helpful was trying to have some bigger  bowl that I'm shooting towards so it  could be a numerical there could be a  lifestyle goal maybe you want to reach  the next X amount of dollars or you want  to be able to travel the world just just  try to imagine a lifestyle that you want  to go after and try to get to the point  of frustration so the first part is  getting motivated by knowing you're  helping people and seeing the feedback  that comes in the second one is getting  motivated by being frustrated with where  you are now if it's really painful your  situation now if you can make it  extremely painful you're more likely to  take action and to want to change your  situation so if your goal is to you know  go to Europe for a month or whatever it  is it doesn't have to be a massive goal  then think about what you're doing now  you know will what you're doing now help  you achieve that goal or not right if  you and if it's not then if you get  angry enough at it know if he's thinking  you know if I'm not working now  I'm not putting my best into it now I'm  never going to be able to achieve the  lifestyle that I want and that will  hopefully give you enough frustration to  take action and go out and do you know  what you need to do to grow your  business and I find that at least for me  at the beginning I had to reset every  day you know I could get motivated for  the day and then I wake up the next day  and you're back into your typical  patterns and I got to get motivated  again now luckily again for me I get a  lot of feedback every day that comes in  I just have to open up my email or look  at the comments on YouTube or Facebook  and see all the glowing review is not  getting me kick-started for what I want  to do for the day if you don't have that  yet then you know you want to start to  try to remember the best points and also  try to get frustrated at your current  situation and how you want to really  improve it and make it better so  hopefully not too long-winded an answer  to the question but a very important  question I hope it helped you dieter for  those are you watching again I'd love to  see the thumbs up come in and makes me  want to do more of these videos and I'd  love to hear we have to think about this  video or if you have a question for your  own company so if we leave in the  comments below it means a lot to me I  always read them every day and hopefully  you'll leave one if you really enjoyed  this video so thank you and I'll see you  on the next episode  you  you
 

